From: LuneOS
Subject: [PATCH] DeviceInfoImpl: publish the display metrics once they are known

The tvDeviceInfo object - PalmSystem.deviceInfo on the client side - is built
once, at the end of DeviceInfoImpl::Initialize(). At that point the display
size is not known: InitDisplayInfo() takes it from the HardwareScreenWidth /
HardwareScreenHeight device-info keys, which nothing in the tree ever sets,
and otherwise falls back to GetDisplayWidth(), reading a DisplayWidth key that
is only populated later by WebAppManager::SetUiSize() when a window appears.
Initialize() runs at startup, before any window exists, so it reads zeroes and
bakes them in: every application on the image sees screenWidth: 0.

Move the object into UpdateTvDeviceInfo() and republish it from the
SetDisplayWidth/SetDisplayHeight overrides, so the values are corrected as
soon as the compositor reports a size.

Publish it before the locale block rather than after, too - that block returns
early when localeInfo cannot be parsed, which would otherwise leave
PalmSystem.deviceInfo unset entirely.

While here, add the remaining fields LunaSysMgr reported and legacy
applications read: maximumCardWidth, maximumCardHeight, keyboardAvailable and
keyboardSlider. Mojo derives its menu row count from maximumCardHeight and
lands on NaN without it, which leaves the application menu unstyled.

touchableRows is deliberately not added. It selects one of Mojo's stylesheet
variants rather than describing the device, and the only variant that ships
artwork is the seven-row one, so an honest number taken from a large display
would leave the menu worse off than a fixed value applied framework-side.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [LuneOS specific; completes 0005]

--- a/src/webos/device_info_impl.cc
+++ b/src/webos/device_info_impl.cc
@@ -31,6 +31,11 @@
 void DeviceInfoImpl::Initialize() {
   GatherInfo();
 
+  // Published here rather than at the end of this function: the locale block
+  // below returns early when localeInfo cannot be parsed, which would leave
+  // PalmSystem.deviceInfo unset altogether.
+  UpdateTvDeviceInfo();
+
   const std::string& json_string =
       util::ReadFile("/var/luna/preferences/localeInfo");
   if (!json_string.empty()) {
@@ -59,6 +64,9 @@
   SetDeviceInfo("SmartServiceCountry", smartservicecountry.c_str());
   }
 
+}
+
+void DeviceInfoImpl::UpdateTvDeviceInfo() {
   Json::Value deviceInfo_json(Json::objectValue);
   deviceInfo_json["modelName"] = model_name_;
   deviceInfo_json["platformVersion"] = platform_version_;
@@ -76,11 +84,38 @@
   }
   deviceInfo_json["screenWidth"] = screen_width_;
   deviceInfo_json["screenHeight"] = screen_height_;
+
+  // LunaSysMgr reported the card area next to the screen size and legacy
+  // frameworks lay themselves out from it. A full-screen card is the display;
+  // the shell takes its own system UI out of that.
+  deviceInfo_json["maximumCardWidth"] = screen_width_;
+  deviceInfo_json["maximumCardHeight"] = screen_height_;
+
+  // Also reported by LunaSysMgr, and read by legacy applications.
+  deviceInfo_json["keyboardAvailable"] = false;
+  deviceInfo_json["keyboardSlider"] = false;
   // deviceInfo_json["panelType"] = "";
 
   SetDeviceInfo("TvDeviceInfo", util::JsonToString(deviceInfo_json));
 }
 
+// The display size is not known when Initialize() runs. HardwareScreenWidth /
+// HardwareScreenHeight are never set by anything, and the DisplayWidth
+// fallback is only filled in by WebAppManager::SetUiSize() once a window
+// exists. Republish whenever it lands, or PalmSystem.deviceInfo keeps the
+// zeroes it was built with and every application reads screenWidth: 0.
+void DeviceInfoImpl::SetDisplayWidth(int value) {
+  DeviceInfo::SetDisplayWidth(value);
+  screen_width_ = static_cast<int>(value / screen_density_);
+  UpdateTvDeviceInfo();
+}
+
+void DeviceInfoImpl::SetDisplayHeight(int value) {
+  DeviceInfo::SetDisplayHeight(value);
+  screen_height_ = static_cast<int>(value / screen_density_);
+  UpdateTvDeviceInfo();
+}
+
 bool DeviceInfoImpl::GetInfoFromLunaPrefs(const char* key,
                                           std::string& value) const {
   char* str = nullptr;
--- a/src/webos/device_info_impl.h
+++ b/src/webos/device_info_impl.h
@@ -25,7 +25,12 @@
 
   void Initialize() override;
 
+  void SetDisplayWidth(int value) override;
+  void SetDisplayHeight(int value) override;
+
  private:
+  void UpdateTvDeviceInfo();
+
   int screen_width_ = 0;
   int screen_height_ = 0;
 
